              "type": "text",
              "text": "A solar eclipse occurs when the Moon passes between the Earth and the Sun, temporarily blocking the Sun's light. This alignment can cause partial, total, or annular eclipses, depending on the distances between these celestial bodies. During a total solar eclipse, the Sun is completely obscured by the Moon, casting a shadow on parts of the Earth and briefly turning day into night."
